cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DART, please cite it as below."
title: "DART: Distributional Auditing of Retrieval Transfer"
abstract: >-
  DART ranks candidate drugs for a heterogeneous single-cell population by a
  population-to-population distance rather than a mean-signature match, and is
  used as a probe to expose when distributional information is trustworthy and
  when objective-aligned evaluation metrics are circular. Its headline finding is
  that apparent distributional gains do not transfer to oracle-independent
  criteria.
authors:
  - name: "Boom5426"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Boom5426/DART"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - single-cell
  - drug retrieval
  - distributional distance
  - perturbation
  - evaluation
